INSERT INTO `aw_blog` (`post_id`, `title`, `post_content`, `status`, `created_time`, `update_time`, `identifier`, `user`, `update_user`, `meta_keywords`, `meta_description`, `comments`, `tags`, `short_content`) VALUES
(1, '10 Best Essential Oils for Aromatherapy to Begin With!!', '<div class=\"col-md-12 gal-pd\">\r\n<div class=\"pro-box\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-6 col-xs-6 pro-mar\">\r\n<h1>10 Best Essential Oils for Aromatherapy to Begin With!!</h1>\r\n<p>If you have decided to step into the world of natural products and are confused about where to start, then the perfect and best way to begin your journey is with essential oils. Instead of drooling over chemical-based cosmetics, if you want a permanent solution to your problems, then switching to the natural way is the best thing to go with. In this sequence, avoiding cosmetics at once will be a difficult task. So, there are aromatherapy essential oils that can be the savior for you in a world full of artificiality.</p>\r\n<p>Before diving into the range of essential oils, one should have enough knowledge about what aromatherapy actually is! So, it is a therapy that uses naturally extracted oils called essential oils for healing, treating, and enhancing the health of the body, mind, and spirit. If you are not feeling the right way and your mind is full of non-relevant thoughts, then aromatherapy is the best solution for you to go with. This therapy consists of massaging with a lotion or oil that contains essential oils in it. The main purpose is to inhale the relaxing and sedative aroma of these naturally produced oils through the skin.</p>\r\n<p>Now, after knowing about aromatherapy, the next thought that comes to mind is the types of oil that one should have in the daily care routine. For this, here is a compiled list that has some exotic essential oils that can be used for aromatherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>1. Lavender Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"lavender essential oil\" height=\"386\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/lavender-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"676\" /></div>\r\n<p>The most recommended and widely used essential oil for aromatherapy is this <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/lavender-essential-oil.html\"><strong>lavender oil</strong></a>. Loaded with amazing properties and a soothing scent; this oil can be used in promoting relaxation and sound sleep. Just combine with a carrier oil like coconut or olive oil and you can directly use this oil for the aromatherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>2. Peppermint Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"peppermint essential oil\" height=\"389\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/peppermint-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"680\" /></div>\r\n<p>Peppermint is the love of all and so does the <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/peppermint-essential-oil.html\">peppermint essential oil</a>. It has a refreshing minty smell that is perfect for summer nights to get relaxed and calm. Not only summers, one can use this oil in winter for treating a sore throat. This oil also works well in reducing anxiety, stress, and fatigue which makes it a perfect option for aromatherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>3. Lemon Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Lemon Essential Oil\" height=\"393\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/lemon-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"688\" /></div>\r\n<p>After reading the name of lemon, the first thought that came to mind is something clean and fresh. This <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/lemon-oil.html\">lemon essential oil</a> is one that can be included in daily life for many of its benefits like promoting a healthy stomach and digestion, killing germs, freshening the air, and of course, making your skin even-toned.</p>\r\n<h2>4. Eucalyptus Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Eucalyptus Essential Oil\" height=\"401\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/eucalyptus-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"702\" /></div>\r\n<p>If you are suffering from a cold and cough, then this <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/lemon-oil.html\">essential oil</a> can is a savior for you. Just pour a few drops of this oil into the diffuser filled with water and inhale its aroma before going to bed. This fights congestion and winter infection, making you able to breathe properly.</p>\r\n<h2>5. Tea Tree Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Tea Tree Essential Oil\" height=\"401\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/tea-tree-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"703\" /></div>\r\n<p>In the sequence of these <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/tea-tree-essential-oil.html\">essential oils</a>, it is the one that has an indefinite number of medicinal properties. From treating dandruff to killing mouth germs and healing acne; you can use this oil in many ways. So, just add it to the list of daily routines and you are all sorted for a relaxing life.</p>\r\n<h2>6. Chamomile Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Chamomile Essential Oil\" height=\"395\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/chamomile-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"692\" /></div>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/chamomile-morocco-essential-oil.html\">This essential oil</a> has an amazing smell that everyone enjoys. Its relaxing and pleasant aroma is something that can help you in getting rid of anxiety, stress, and fatigue promoting sound sleep. With this, it also fights bacterial infection and digestive problems, and overall it promotes youthful younger-looking skin.</p>\r\n<h2>7. Rosemary Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Rosemary Essential Oil\" height=\"402\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/rosemary-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"704\" /></div>\r\n<p>This is a multi-purpose oil that has many uses. If you are having a digestive problem, then applying <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/rosemary-essential-oil.html\">this oil</a> to the abdominal area will help in curing the problem. Also, if one is suffering from sore muscles, then also messaging with this oil can works well. If in case of cough, cold, and depression; this oil can be used in diffusers for congestion and blocked nose. All these uses prove that this oil is the best one to go with without having second thoughts.</p>\r\n<h2>8. Sweet Orange Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Sweet Orange Essential Oil\" height=\"407\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/sweet-orange-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"712\" /></div>\r\n<p>If you are frustrated with the problem of lack of sleep, then <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/sweet-orange-essential-oil.html\">sweet orange essential oil</a> is the best option to drool over. It has amazing properties that can uplift your mood by reducing anxiety and hypertension. Apart from its sedative aroma, it is the one that also works well in fighting infectious bacteria and boosting the immune system.</p>\r\n<h2>9. Marjoram Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Marjoram Essential Oil\" height=\"409\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/marjoram-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"716\" /></div>\r\n<p>This <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/marjoram-oil.html\">oil</a> when blended with a <strong>carrier oil</strong>, reduces depression and anxiety like a spellbound. You can use it in many ways like applying it on the back of the neck to reduce stress and tension. With this, it can also be used in a diffuser for the inhaling purpose to infuse the positive vibes in the room.</p>\r\n<h2>10. Grapefruit Essential Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Grapefruit Essential Oil\" height=\"406\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/grapefruit-essential-oil-img.jpg\"}}\" width=\"711\" /></div>\r\n<p>This <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/grapefruit-essential-oil.html\">essential oil</a> is one of the most popular and widely used oils from the citrus family. If you are feeling jet lag, then the spicy and refreshing aroma of this oil can make you feel relaxed by calming the tensed nerves of the brain. You can also diffuse its amazing and attractive aroma into your room through a diffuser.</p>\r\n<p>All the above-mentioned essential oils will take your skin-care routine to a whole new level. So, don\'t stress yourself and pick any one of the listed products to ginger up your skin-care. Now, you also don\'t need to compromise with the quality of the products as many online portals are bonding up with <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\"><strong>essential oil manufacturers and suppliers</strong></a> to provide customers the utmost satisfaction of online shopping.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<style><!--\r\n.u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b { padding:0px; margin: 0; padding-top:1em!important; padding-bottom:1em!important; width:100%; display: block; font-weight:bold; background-color:inherit; border:0!important; border-left:4px solid #3498DB!important; text-decoration:none; } .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b:active, .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b:hover { opacity: 1; transition: opacity 250ms; webkit-transition: opacity 250ms; text-decoration:none; } .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b { transition: background-color 250ms; webkit-transition: background-color 250ms; opacity: 1; transition: opacity 250ms; webkit-transition: opacity 250ms; } .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b .ctaText { font-weight:bold; color:#F39C12; text-decoration:none; font-size: 16px; } .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b .postTitle { color:#27AE60; text-decoration: underline!important; font-size: 16px; } .u804d29a47d4f46c3e93c3d3a7718604b:hover .postTitle { text-decoration: underline!important; }\r\n--></style>', 1, '2022-02-18 11:45:44', '2022-12-12 10:36:15', '10-best-essential-oils-for-aromatherapy', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', 'naturesnaturalindia blog', 0, '', '<p>If you have decided to step in the world of natural products and is confused from where to start, then the most perfect and the best way to begin your journey is with essential oils. Instead of drooling over the chemical-based cosmetics, if you want a permanent solution to your problems, then switching to the natural way is the best thing to go with. In this sequence, avoiding cosmetics at once will be a difficult task. So, there are aromatherapy essential oils that can be the savior for you in the world full of artificiality.</p>\r\n<p>Before diving into the range of essential oils, one should have enough knowledge about what aromatherapy actually is! So, it is a therapy that uses the naturally extracted oils called essential oils for healing, treating, and enhancing the health of body, mind, and spirit. If you are not feeling in the right way and your mind is full of non-relevant thoughts, then aromatherapy is the best solution for you to go with. This therapy consists of massaging with the lotion or oil that contains essential oils in it. The main purpose is to inhale the relaxing and sedative aroma of these naturally produced oils through the skin.</p>'),
(2, '10 Exotic Certified Organic Oils to Pamper Yourself Naturally!!', '<div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-6 col-xs-6 pro-mar\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<h1>10 Exotic Certified Organic Oils to Pamper Yourself Naturally!!</h1>\r\n<p>Using <strong>organic and certified</strong> things has become the basic mantra of everyone nowadays who is a little worried about the rapid change in the environmental conditions that require a quick change in lifestyle as well. And, for this, one can begin with skincare products taking good care of your skin is indeed one of the most required things to do when the environmental conditions are not favorable.</p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Exotic Certified Organic Oils\" height=\"407\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/exotic-certified-organic-oils.jpg\"}}\" width=\"712\" /></div>\r\n<p>Keeping this in mind, <strong>Naturesnaturalindia.com</strong> is again here to solve the problems of everyone related to personal care and well-being. And, this time, we are here with our wide range of certified organic essential oils as these oils are not extracted organically but also the plants or the herbs from which these oils are extracted are also grown and harvested organically and without the use of any chemical substitutes so that the benefits of <strong>certified organic oils</strong> for healthy living body and mind are indeed commendable.</p>\r\n<p>Here, we have listed the top 10 <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/certified-organic-oils.html\">certified organic essential oils</a> so that when you are about to choose one from the list, you can be sure about the benefits and uses of these oils so that you can get the best one for yourself. So, without wasting any more time, let us get started with the <strong>certified organic essential oils</strong>:</p>\r\n<h2>1. Organic Aloe Vera Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Aloe Vera certified organic oil\" height=\"513\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/aloe-vera-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"724\" /></div>\r\n<p><strong>General Uses</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Aloe Vera is known to have moisturizing properties that can moisturize and hydrate the skin naturally.<br />2. This certified organic gel can also be used to support a healthy and fit digestive system.<br />3. It can also reduce harmful toxins from the blood and can purify it.<br />4. When massaged on the infected area, this can also be used to soothe muscle &amp; joint pain.<br />5. This gel is used in the manufacturing of certain skincare and make-up products.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Benefits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Aloe vera gel is having many amazing properties like antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, antibacterial, antiviral, antifungal, and stimulating ones that make it very useful. the gel is also known to have numerous therapeutic benefits that make it an aromatherapy substitute as well&nbsp;When applied topically, it can soothe various issues related to skin and hair the headache can also be cured when using natural Aloe Vera.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Blends Well with</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Coconut oil<br />2. Olive oil<br />3. Juniper berry essential oil<br />4. Thyme essential oil<br />5. Ylang Ylang essential oil</p>\r\n<h2>2. Organic&nbsp;Black Pepper Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Black pepper certified organic oil\" height=\"500\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/black-pepper-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"706\" /></div>\r\n<p><strong>General Uses</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Black pepper-certified organic oil is having various properties like antiseptic, antibacterial, antifungal, anti-inflammatory, and stimulating ones as well which make it super amazing and beneficial.<br />2. Those who are having the problem of smoking can use this oil as it can control cigarette cravings.<br />3. It also helps to detoxify the body naturally.<br />4. For the past many years, it has been used as a natural food preservative.<br />5. The antibacterial and antiviral properties of this oil are helpful to eliminate various viruses and bacteria effectively and naturally.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Benefits</strong></p>\r\n<p>This oil is very helpful to improve blood circulation&nbsp;When massaged on the infected area, this oil can be helpful to ease muscle and joint pain. having a spicy tint of strong aroma, this oil is used in aromatherapy sessions&nbsp;It can also be used to uplift mood naturally when diffused around&nbsp;Patients with insomnia or depression can use this oil to reduce their symptoms.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Blends Well with</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Rosemary essential oil<br />2. Cypress essential oil<br />3. Bergamot essential oil<br />4. Clary sage essential oil<br />5. Clove essential oil<br />6. Fennel seed essential oil</p>\r\n<h2>3. Organic Coffee Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Coffee bean certified organic oil\" height=\"491\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/coffee-bean-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"694\" /></div>\r\n<p><strong>General Uses</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. This oil is also helpful in reducing acne and pimples effectively.<br />2. Having anti-allergic properties, this oil is well-suited for every skin type for topical application.<br />3. The antibacterial and antiviral properties are helpful to eliminate viral and bacterial growth in the body.<br />4. This oil is also effective in boosting immune health.<br />5. Also, hair-related and skin-related problems can be cured easily with this oil.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Benefits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Coffee bean oil is known to have amazing therapeutic benefits that make it more useful and beneficial the crisp aroma of this oil can be used to prevent chronic diseases respiratory health can also be improved by inhaling the aroma of this certified oil. patients with insomnia can also use this oil to reduce the symptoms those who want to refresh themselves can inhale the aroma of this oil as it is a great stress reliever.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Blends Well with</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Bergamot essential oil<br />2. Cedarwood essential oil<br />3. Lemon essential oil<br />4. Orange essential oil<br />5. Thyme essential oil</p>\r\n<h2>4. Organic Lavender oil</h2>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Lavender certified organic oil\" height=\"505\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/lavender-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"712\" /></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<div align=\"center\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<p><strong>General Uses</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. This certified organic oil is also having various medicinal properties and hence, is used in the formulation of various medicines<br />2. This oil is known for its amazing and soothing aroma all over the world<br />3. Minor burns and cuts can be treated very well by using this oil<br />4. All who are having chapped or dry skin and body parts can use this oil<br />5. Because of its pleasing and soothing aroma, this oil is used in the production of perfumes and scents.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Benefits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Lavender oil is the most widely used aromatherapy oil because of its amazing therapeutic properties lavender essential oil is known to have a calming effect both physically and emotionally when the aroma of this oil is diffused around, it works as a great stress reliever. patients with insomnia can use this oil effectively as it promotes sound sleep the issues of depression and anxiety can be easily cured with the aroma of this oil.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Blends Well with</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Rose essential oil<br />2. Pine essential oil<br />3. Lemon essential oil<br />4. Clary sage essential oil</p>\r\n<h2>5. Organic Olive Oil</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div align=\"center\"></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\"></div>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Olive certified organic oil\" height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/olive-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"689\" /></div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><strong>General Uses</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Olive oil is known to have so many beneficial properties that are used for many medicinal purposes.<br />2. This oil can also be used as a makeup remover.<br />3. Having moisturizing properties, it works as the best hair oil for providing the required nutrients to your hair.<br />4. Olive oil is widely used as a carrier oil or base oil to blend other essential oils.<br />5. The problem of body dryness in winter can also be solved with the topical application of this oil.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Benefits</strong></p>\r\n<p>This carrier oil is used in the manufacturing of certain skincare products like moisturizers, make-up removers, creams, and lotions. this oil can also be used to cure large pores on the face. olive oil can work wonders in reducing dark spots. the application of olive oil is also helpful in reducing belly fat. the therapeutic properties of this oil make it an aromatherapy oil as well.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Blends Well with</strong></p>\r\n<p>1. Cedarwood essential oil<br />2. Juniper berry essential oil<br />3. Clary sage essential oil<br />4. Lemon balm essential oil</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2>6. Organic Eucalyptus Oil</h2>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Eucalyptus certified organic oil\" height=\"496\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/eucalyptus-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"699\" /></div>\r\n<h3></h3>\r\n<h3>General Uses</h3>\r\n1. Eucalyptus oil is having so many properties that it is being used in various fields.<br />2. The oil can also be used in perfume manufacturing because of its refreshing and soothing aroma<br />3. It is considered amazing for the skin and hence, it is used in the manufacturing of certain cosmetic products.<br />4. Having antiseptic properties, this oil can also be used to heal wounds and cuts naturally.<br />5. When applied topically on any wound blended with a carrier oil, it speeds up the wound healing process<br />\r\n<h3>Therapeutic Benefits</h3>\r\nOrganic eucalyptus oil is known for its aroma worldwide and is loaded with therapeutic benefits. this oil can be used to cure insomnia the problem of stress, anxiety, and hypertension can also be reduced by having therapeutic properties, this oil is also used as amazing aromatherapy oil the issues of headaches and depression can also be treated with the aroma of this oil.<br />\r\n<h3>Blends Well With</h3>\r\n1. Cedarwood essential oil<br />2. Ginger essential oil<br />3. Lavender essential oil<br />4. Juniper essential oil<br />5. Cypress essential oil<br />6. Rose essential oil<br />7. Pine essential oil<br />8. Thyme essential oil<br />9. Peppermint essential oil</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-6 col-xs-6 pro-mar\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<h2>7. Organic Frankincense Oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Frankincense certified organic oil\" height=\"515\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/frankincense-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"727\" /></div>\r\n<h3>General Uses</h3>\r\n1. Frankincense oil is known worldwide for its soothing and pleasing aroma.<br />2. This certified organic oil can also be used as an ointment to treat cuts or wounds naturally<br />3. Having antiviral, antibacterial, and antifungal properties, this oil can be used for healing infectious diseases<br />4. This oil can also boost the immune system and can prevent the body from getting affected by various diseases.<br />5. When applied topically with a carrier oil, this oil can reduce stretch-marks<br />6. The problem of acne and scars can be cured with this oil<br />\r\n<h3>Therapeutic Properties</h3>\r\nFrankincense certified organic oil is one of the best aromatherapy oils when rubbed on the temples of the forehead, it can calm the tensed nerves&nbsp;when rubbed on the wrists, and it can work as a natural perfume. when the aroma of this oil is diffused in the surroundings, it can uplift the mood effectively and naturally<br />problem of insomnia can also be treated with this oil<br />\r\n<h3>Blends Well With</h3>\r\n1. Lavender essential oil<br />2. Geranium essential oil<br />3. Rose essential oil<br />4. Sandalwood essential oil<br />5. Ylang-Ylang essential oil<br />6. Orange essential oil<br />7. Lemon essential oil<br />\r\n<h2>8. Clove Bud certified organic oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Clove Bud certified organic oil\" height=\"606\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/clove-bud-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"855\" /></div>\r\n<h3>General Uses</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Having numerous health benefits, this oil can be used to aid digestive problems</li>\r\n<li>Having amazing properties, this certified organic oil can be used to make certain skincare products.</li>\r\n<li>It also works well as an insect repellent</li>\r\n<li>Clove bud oil is also used for its moisturizing properties to cure the problem of dry skin</li>\r\n<li>This oil can also be used to remove stains and marks from metal like swords and medals.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Therapeutic Benefits</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Having properties like antiseptic, antifungal, antiviral, antibacterial, anti-inflammatory, stimulating, and antispasmodic ones; this oil is very amazing.</li>\r\n<li>This oil is also used in the aromatherapy sessions because of its soothing aroma</li>\r\n<li>When the aroma is diffused in the surroundings, it works as a mood lifter</li>\r\n<li>When blended with a carrier oil, it can be used as an aromatherapy oil as well</li>\r\n<li>The issues of depression, anxiety, insomnia, hypertension, and stress can be reduced effectively with this oil</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Blends Well With</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Basil essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Lemon essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Orange essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Bergamot essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Cinnamon Bark essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Rose essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Rosemary essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Clary Sage essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Ylang Ylang essential oil</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>9. Geranium certified organic oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Geranium certified organic oil\" height=\"606\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/geranium-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"855\" /></div>\r\n<h3>General Uses</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Geranium oil is being used traditionally to promote healthy skin with a healthy mind</li>\r\n<li>The amazing properties of this oil can be used to rejuvenate the skin naturally</li>\r\n<li>When applied topically on this skin, this oil is used to regulate oil production.</li>\r\n<li>This oil can also be used to prevent the harmful bacteria on the injuries</li>\r\n<li>The anti-inflammatory properties of this oil work wonder in treating cuts, rashes, redness, swelling, etc.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Therapeutic Benefits</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Geranium oil is known to have numerous therapeutic properties that make it an aromatherapy oil</li>\r\n<li>This oil can also be used to boost the immunity of the body.</li>\r\n<li>The aroma of this amazing oil is helpful to maintain blood pressure</li>\r\n<li>The use of this oil can also eliminate the issues of insomnia</li>\r\n<li>The problem of depression and anxiety can also be solved by the application of this oil</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Blends Well With</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Clary sage essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Lemon balm essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Juniper berry essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Olive oil</li>\r\n<li>Coconut oil</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>10. Jojoba certified organic oil</h2>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Jojoba certified organic oil\" height=\"606\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/jojoba-certified-organic-oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"855\" /></div>\r\n<h3>General Uses</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jojoba Oil is an amazing natural makeup remover</li>\r\n<li>This certified oil can also be used as a natural and chemical-free home cleaner.</li>\r\n<li>When applied topically blended with a carrier oil, this oil can also control the oil secretions by the skin.</li>\r\n<li>Because of the stimulating properties, this oil can also be used to treat cuts, burns, bruises, and other wounds</li>\r\n<li>The antiseptic property of this oil can speed up the wound healing process.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Therapeutic Properties</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jojoba oil is an amazing carrier oil that is used to form advantageous aromatherapy blends with essential oils.</li>\r\n<li>This oil is also having therapeutic properties can it can be used to treat depression issues</li>\r\n<li>Jojoba certified oil is also used in various scents and perfumes formulation</li>\r\n<li>This oil also works as a mood lifter when diffused around the room</li>\r\n<li>Could not sleep at night, inhale and you will have a sound sleep.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Blends Well With</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Rose essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Rosemary essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Clary Sage essential oil</li>\r\n<li>Ylang Ylang essential oil</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Excited!!! Well, don&rsquo;t let this excitement fade as on Naturesnaturalindia.com, you will get the best and good quality certified organic essential oils as we are recognized as the <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/\">best essential oils manufacturer</a> all across India. So, without ant worries, just check out the website and have a look at our wide range and drooling catalogs that will take you to the world of nature.</p>\r\n<p>Take Care of Yourself Naturally with Naturesnaturalindia.com!!!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>General Uses<br />This certified organic oil is also having various medicinal properties and hence, is used in the formulation of various medicinesThis oil is known for its amazing and soothing aroma all over the worldMinor burns and cuts can be treated very well by using this oilFor all who are having chapped or dry skin and body parts, can use this oilBecause of its pleasing and soothing aroma, this oil is used in the production of perfumes and scents.<br />Therapeutic Benefits<br />Lavender oil is the most widely used aromatherapy oil because of its amazing therapeutic propertiesLavender essential oil is known to have a calming effect both physically and emotionallyWhen the aroma of this oil is diffused around, it works as a great stress reliever.Patients of insomnia can use this oil effectively as it promotes sound sleepThe issues of depression and anxiety can be easily cured with the aroma of this oil<br />Blends Well with<br />Rose essential oilPine essential oilLemon essential oilClary sage essential oilOrganic Olive Oil</p>', 1, '2022-02-18 11:51:57', '2022-12-12 10:37:06', 'exotic-certified-organic-oils-to-pamper-yourself', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p>Using organic and certified things has become the basic mantra of everyone nowadays who is a little worried about the rapid change in the environmental conditions that require a quick change in lifestyle as well. And, for this, one can begin with skincare products taking good care of your skin is indeed one of the most required things to do when the environmental conditions are not favorable.</p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img alt=\"Exotic Certified Organic Oils\" height=\"448\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/exotic-certified-organic-oils.jpg\"}}\" width=\"879\" /></div>'),
(3, 'Coffee Oil - Its Derivation, Variants, Properties, and Usage', '<h1 class=\"normal\"><strong><img alt=\"History And Cultivation Of Coffee Trees\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/History_And_Cultivation_Of_Coffee_Trees.jpg\"}}\" title=\"History And Cultivation Of Coffee Trees\" /></strong></h1>\r\n<h2 class=\"normal\"><strong>History and Cultivation of Coffee Trees</strong></h2>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">When people think about coffee, they feel the aroma and flavor of the coffee immediately due to its familiarity. However, before the 15th century, it was not a known commodity. Yemen began its cultivation in the Arabian Peninsula during the 15th century. Coffee became a popular energizing beverage in Mecca and Constantinople, coffeehouses flourished, and its trade expanded.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">People in Persia, Turkey, Syria, and Egypt naturalized coffee cultivation by the 16th century. Coffee cultivation began in Europe after much resistance from&nbsp; European religious communities, and by the end of the 17th century, it became a featured beverage with breakfast in Britain and America. Coffee cultivation expanded to the Indonesian archipelago and USA in the 18th century. The Caribbean, South, and Central America became the coffee trading hubs, and the pendulum of production shifted from Yemen to America by the 19th century. It is said that coffee output in America has originated from one coffee tree in the Dutch botanical garden. &nbsp;During the 20th century, Brazil topped coffee production charts with extensive cultivation of Coffea arabica species.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The coffee tree is an evergreen plant that reaches a maximum height of 15 feet. It bears glossy leaves and small white flowers that turn into fruit. The plant grows well in a climate that has 23 to 28-degree temperatures, average rainfall of 60-80 inches, and a dry period of 2-3 months. The planters sow it at the beginning of the rainy season, and the coffee plants begin to produce fruit during the third to fifth year. The plants need frequent trimming, weeding, and fertilization with little or no shading for a healthy crop. The fruit turns reddish-purple within seven to nine months. The coffee fruits or cherries contain two raw seeds.&nbsp; For the harvest of coffee beans, the farmers prefer selective picking, which is a meticulous affair.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Coffee Beans and Coffee Oil Extraction</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Coffee Beans And Coffee Oil Extraction\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Coffee_Beans_And_Coffee_Oil_Extraction.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Coffee Beans And Coffee Oil Extraction\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">After harvesting coffee cherries, the essential oil manufacturers clean them with water and sundry. They extract oils from the roasted beans and green beans. The unroasted green beans are soft and emit a slightly grassy aroma, while roasted beans have a characteristically rich coffee aroma and aroma due to chemical changes mooted by roasting. The roasted beans lose moisture and expand physically. Roasted coffee beans contain less caffeine than beans.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The flavor profile of coffee beans or powder depends on the temperature and duration of the roasting process and pre-treatment of beans. The coffee makers can produce different coffee variants with diverse caffeine concentrations.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>pure essential oil manufacturers</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>cold press the beans soon after roasting to preserve the potency of the aroma and extract coffee oil. Shared similar chemical constituents are flavonoids and fatty acids such as linoleic, palmitic, oleic, and stearic acid. Coffee oil has anti-inflammatory properties that reduce soreness in muscles and puffiness around the eyes. Besides, it elevates mood, stimulates appetite, supports the immune system, and repairs the skin damage caused by UV rays, free radicals, and aging.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Functions of Each Constituent in Coffee Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Flavonoids </strong>- They minimize the effects of free radicals, rejuvenate the skin cells and reduce inflammation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Linoleic Acid </strong>- It moisturizes the skin, delays aging signs, improves appearance, and promotes skin cell regeneration.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Palmitic Acid</strong> - It soothes skin abrasions, and heals rashes, dryness, and insect bites on the skin. It removes excess oil from the skin.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Oleic Acid </strong>-&nbsp; The acid neutralizes the effect of air pollutants with antioxidants and reduces irritation, redness, and scars.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Stearic Acid </strong>- It acts as a cleanser, removes dark spots, and helps maintain the texture of the skin formulation. It repairs damaged skin.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A Brief of Green Coffee Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"A Brief Of Green Coffee Oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/A_Brief_Of_Green_Coffee_Oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"A Brief Of Green Coffee Oil\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">Green coffee oil extracted from unroasted beans is yellow to a light brown, dense, smooth, and viscous oil. It is odorless or has a slightly green, herbal aroma. The oil is high in fatty acids, flavonoids, and vitamins.&nbsp; It is rich in antioxidants and helps reduce the appearance of cellulite. Its topical application cleanses and softens the skin, giving it brightness.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">Green coffee oil may appear cloudy due to its natural wax content. The users can keep the container or bottle of the oil in hot water for a few minutes to get clear oil.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A Brief of Roasted Coffee Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The fatty oil obtained from the roasted beans is green to dark brown and possesses the signature coffee aroma. It contains lecithin and vitamin E, making it a perfect ingredient for dermal formulations. The oil protects the skin from constant wetting or drying and hides unpleasant odors.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: georgia, palatino;\"><strong>Suitability For Use </strong>- Coffee oil is a cold-pressed fatty acid oil, but its properties are more similar to essential oils. Both the oils are excellent as an ingredient in massage creams, body lotions, lip balms, bar soaps, sun protection formulations, hair oils or masks, and conditioners. Green coffee beans oil adds a pleasant aroma that complements citrus aromas flawlessly in a perfume. Roasted coffee oil is largely used in under-eye formulations, body scrubs, cosmetic butters, diffuser blends, and skin scrubs.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommended Uses of Coffee Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Recommended Uses Of Coffee Oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Recommended_Uses_Of_Coffee_Oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Recommended Uses Of Coffee Oil\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; text-align: justify; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The scent of coffee is adaptable in fragrance formulations as it blends well with a variety of aromatic woody, resinous, spicy, tobacco, and leather essences. Fragrance makers use it in masculine perfumes, skincare, and grooming products.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; text-align: justify; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">People exposed to powerful odors as part of their profession or hobby can use roasted coffee oil to work as an olfactory cleanser. The coffee oil removes lingering odors.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; text-align: justify; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The users can apply the green coffee oil as a regular night serum to tighten the skin and improve appearance. They can combine it with sweet almond or olive oil for facial or hair massage purposes. The same blend can be used to apply under the eyes to reduce puffiness.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; text-align: justify; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">The food courts, event organizers, and restaurants can use the combination of vanilla oil and coffee oil in a diffuser in food areas.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; text-align: justify; font-family: georgia, palatino;\">Aromatherapists can add it to their blends, meant for skin-rejuvenating purposes and under-eye treatment.</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia, palatino; font-size: medium;\">India also produces coffee crops substantially, so there is a significant presence of </span><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/coffee-oil.html\" style=\"font-family: georgia, palatino; font-size: medium;\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>coffee oil wholesale suppliers </strong></a><span style=\"font-family: georgia, palatino; font-size: medium;\">and manufacturers in India.&nbsp;</span></p>', 1, '2022-03-24 10:01:30', '2025-01-25 07:00:15', 'Coffee-Oil-Its-Derivation-Variants-Properties-and-Usage', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 0, '', '<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"History And Cultivation Of Coffee Trees\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/History_And_Cultivation_Of_Coffee_Trees.jpg\"}}\" title=\"History And Cultivation Of Coffee Trees\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>When people think about coffee, they feel the aroma and flavor of the coffee immediately due to its familiarity. However, before the 15th century, it was not a known commodity. Yemen began its cultivation in the Arabian Peninsula during the 15th century. Coffee became a popular energizing beverage in Mecca and Constantinople, coffeehouses flourished, and its trade expanded.</span></p>');
INSERT INTO `aw_blog` (`post_id`, `title`, `post_content`, `status`, `created_time`, `update_time`, `identifier`, `user`, `update_user`, `meta_keywords`, `meta_description`, `comments`, `tags`, `short_content`) VALUES
(4, 'Advance Your Cosmic and Spiritual Journey with Queer Essential Oils!', '<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><img alt=\"Queer Essential Oils\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Queer_Essential_Oils.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Queer Essential Oils\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Nature is full of bioactive molecules resonating and associated with the infinite cosmos in some ways. Distinct essential oils are highly concentrated natural essence of the respective botanical parts. People have been using them as an integral part of spiritual, cultural, and religious practices across different civilizations in the world. Many essential oils such as Myrrh, Patchouli, Sandalwood, and Spikenard have biblical references. People used these oils for grounding, cleansing, enlightenment, coping with grief, spirituality, and showing gratitude. Their aroma and properties help users assess their alignment with energies and relationships surrounding them, awaken sixth sense, and guide the near ones on the path of light.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">The essential oils for developing cosmic consciousness do not always smell fresh, floral, or lemony with top notes. Most spiritual essential oils have base notes, and the <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>blend creators or essential oil suppliers</strong></a> add some floral or fruity essential oils to it for initial notes. They possess typically woody, resinous, smoky, sweet, and earthy base notes. Their diffusion or application unleashes the unlimited potential of the mind and facilitates alignment between spiritual and worldly pursuits.&nbsp; The resulting deep spiritual connection improves mental clarity, decisiveness, and intuition. Such essential oils are&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Patchouli Essential Oil (Matured Dark)</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Myrrh Oil</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Sandalwood Essential Oil</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Spikenard Essential Oil</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Agarwood/Oud Essential Oil</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Patchouli essential oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Patchouli essential oil is a dark golden brown, medium to thick oil derived by distilling the patchouli (botanical name - Pogostemon cablin) leaves. The matured <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/patchouli-essential-oil.html\"><strong>patchouli essential oil</strong></a> smells intensely earthy and woody.&nbsp; It complements other aromas of diverse essential oils in a blend beautifully. Patchouli oil dilution is an excellent, rich, sultry staple for skin care and hair care.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><img alt=\"Patchouli essential oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Patchouli_essential_oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Patchouli essential oil\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Patchouli oil has calming and grounding effects and works as a fixative in cosmic blends created to awaken the sixth Chakra. Its application between eyebrows helps align the mind and deal with pessimism, uncertainty, and confusion.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Myrrh Essential Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">People have appreciated myrrh resin for its spiritual, fragrance, medicinal, and dermal applications for centuries. <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/myrrh-essential-oil.html\"><strong>Myrrh essential oil manufacturers</strong></a> extract a golden yellow to brown medium-consistency oil obtained from the resin of the myrrh tree (botanical name - Commiphora myrrha) by steam distillation. The oil has a more charming aroma than the resin, and users often use it for room spray, spiritual, and incense purposes. It offers warm, earthy, woody, and balsamic base notes to a blend. The oil is a perfect addition to spiritual and religious fragrances as it helps mellow down the emotional turmoils and balance the mind.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Myrrh essential oil manufacturers\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Myrrh_essential_oil_manufacturers.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Myrrh essential oil manufacturers\" /></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sandalwood Essential Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Sandalwood is the most imitated scent in the world of fragrance due to its rich, mystic, and sweet fragrance. The essential oil derived from sandalwood (botanical name - Santalum album) is medium to thick clear oil with a yellow tinge. It smells warm, sweet, deep, with woody, floral undertones and offers enigmatic long-lasting base notes.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Natural sandalwood essential oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Natural_sandalwood_essential_oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Natural sandalwood essential oil\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Sandalwood essential oil has a soothing effect and imbues a sense of inner peace. Its application or diffusion helps in stress, low self-esteem, sleeplessness, and depression. It unblocks the heart chakra and helps develop loving connections and balanced relationships with self and other creatures. <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/sandalwood-essential-oil.html\" target=\"_self\"><strong>Natural sandalwood essential oil</strong></a> has versatile applications in skin care, perfumes, and spirituality. The users across different cultures diffused or applied it as incense for religious or spiritual purposes. Furthermore, it is an excellent skincare elixir that reduces scars and stretch marks.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Spikenard Essential Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Spikenard essential oil, also known as Jatamansi, Nard, and Muskroot, is a pale amber to greenish amber, medium-consistency oil. The<a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_self\"><strong> essential oil manufacturers</strong></a> obtain it from the roots of the Jatamansi plant found in the Himalayas by steam distillation. The oil smells deep, musky, woody, earthy, and vetiver-like. It has relaxing effects that help in sound sleep.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Spikenard essential oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Spikenard_essential_oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Spikenard essential oil\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Spikenard essential oil is grounding, and it opens up and balances the root chakra. It has been historically used for meditation, communal ceremonies, and other spiritual applications. It goes well with woody, spicy, floral, and herbaceous essential oils.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Agarwood/Oud Essential Oil</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Agarwood oil is dark, gold amber, transparent, viscous oil with a long-lasting, sweet, warm, deep, woody, and smoky aroma. The manufacturers derive it from the matured, resinous heartwood of highly revered and esteemed agarwood trees. The oil also emits ambery incense, honey, and animal-like notes. Its aroma gets sweeter and muskier with aging, and therefore, it is a high worth fragrance to the palette of natural perfume makers and lovers. It evokes a spiritual connection with nature and the cosmos.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Agarwood &amp; Oud Essential Oil\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Agarwood_Oud_Essential_Oil.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Agarwood &amp; Oud Essential Oil\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">People in East India have considered it a sacred oil and used it for ceremonial anointing traditionally. They prefer using this oil as incense and recommend applying it for cosmic journeys and spiritual enlightenment. The oil assimilates the energy and tranquilizes the mind.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">The <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_self\"><strong>essential oil suppliers </strong></a>also make blends using oils for spiritual uses. Some ways to use essential oils for spiritual awakening and progressive journeys are as follow,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">❖&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Add a drop of each essential oil mentioned above to 10 ml jojoba oil. Then massage this mixture with fingers on the middle of the forehead gently.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;❖&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Make a diffuser blend with four drops of agarwood oil, two drops of Roman chamomile oil, and two drops of patchouli oil. Add this blend to 12 ml water in a diffuser and turn it on 10 minutes before meditation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;❖&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Prepare a healing salve with five drops of sandalwood oil, three drops of helichrysum oil, and 10 ml extra virgin olive oil. Apply it to the affected areas.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;❖&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Create a personal fragrance oil by combining 4-5 drops of spikenard oil, two drops of geranium oil, two drops of myrrh oil, rosemary oil, and 1 ml sweet almond oil. Apply this mixture to near ear lobes, middle of the chest, and wrists.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A Note</strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">As an essential oil manufacturer, we advise users not to use these oils for internal consumption. The oils are safe for topical application or diffusion. 100% pure natural sandalwood, agarwood, and spikenard essential oils produced in India are available with Natures Natural India for a non-stop, fulfilling cosmos journey of the users.</span></p>', 1, '2022-04-14 12:05:42', '2025-01-27 07:47:14', 'cosmic-and-spiritual-journey-with-essential-oils', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Queer Essential Oils\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Queer_Essential_Oils.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Queer Essential Oils\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Nature is full of bioactive molecules resonating and associated with the infinite cosmos in some ways. Distinct essential oils are highly concentrated natural essence of the respective botanical parts. People have been using them as an integral part of spiritual, cultural, and religious practices across different civilizations in the world. Many essential oils such as Myrrh, Patchouli, Sandalwood, and Spikenard have biblical references. People used these oils for grounding, cleansing, enlightenment, coping with grief, spirituality, and showing gratitude. Their aroma and properties help users assess their alignment with energies and relationships surrounding them, awaken sixth sense, and guide the near ones on the path of light.</span></p>'),
(5, 'Indian Attars - A Distinguished Rich Fragrance to Treat to The World!', '<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span>Table Content</span></h2>\r\n<div align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<table style=\"width: 366px; height: 312px;\"><colgroup><col width=\"623\" /></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Get To Know Six Attars For Winters!</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>The Traditional Indian Attars For Winters</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Difference between Musk and Black Musk</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Ambergris/Amber Attar</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Saffron Attar</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Rose Attar</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Lily Attar</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Oud Attar</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><img alt=\"Indian Attars\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Indian_Attars_1.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Indian Attars\" /></strong></h2>\r\n<h2 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Get to Know Six Attars for Winters!</strong></h2>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/blog/indian-attars-fragrance-to-treat-to-the-world/\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Traditional Indian Attars</strong></a> hold a special and prized place in the world of perfume due to following reasons</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They are highly concentrated perfume oils prepared after a long maturing process.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They get better with age in terms of aroma.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They are prepared in a base oil - precious sandalwood oil.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They are available in different, extraordinary fragrances.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They do not contain alcohol or any spirit.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">They are 100% made from natural botanicals.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; text-align: justify;\">The perfumers use attar as a base to create new fragrances.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Attar is called &lsquo;Itr&rsquo; in Arabic and &lsquo;Itir&rsquo; in Persian. The attars are classified into two categories - Warm and Cool based on their perceived effect on the human body. Warm attars include black musk, ambergris, and saffron, while cool attars include rose, jasmine, khus, kewda, and mogra. The other attars are frangipani, gulhina, tagetes erecta, honeysuckle, jasmine, kadam, lily, lotus, mitti, night queen, tuberose, and shamama attars.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"></span><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The perfumers in North India make attars as an age-old tradition. They extract attars by distilling the flowers, herbs, and spices in sandalwood oil and maturing it (for 1 to 10 years) by following practices developed centuries ago. Natures Natural India provides many varieties of Indian Attars. Some attars are suitable for winters due to their warmth, and others work well for summers due to their lightness and smell. But overall, Indian attars are a pleasant fragrance treat for the users.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Like other perfumes, the attars are not sprayed. Attars are generally available in tiny crystal bottles and are dabbed with fingers on the wrist, neck, underarms, between chest, near earlobes, and behind knees.</span></p>\r\n<h2 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>The Traditional Indian Attars For Winters</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Black Musk</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"></span><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The flowering plant of black musk (Nardotachys Jatamasi) grows in the Himalayan regions. It bears bell-shaped pink flowers and aromatic underground stems. The flowers and rhizomes are crushed, and hydro-distilled, and matured in sandalwood oil for a period of one to ten years.</span><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Black musk attar\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Black_musk_attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Black musk attar\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/black-musk-attar.html\" target=\"_self\"><strong>Cosmetic grade Black musk attar</strong></a> is an amber-colored thick perfume oil. It is 100% natural oil that produces warming effects during winters and helps deal with winter blues. The users can add it to the lotions, face creams, and shampoos or conditioners for aroma.</span></p>\r\n<h3 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Difference between Musk and Black Musk</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Musk attar is different from black musk oil as sources of fragrances are different. Musk is an aromatic compound found in the organs of Himalayan male deer. But it is rarely available nowadays and so pure musk attar is largely not available.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Ambergris/Amber Attar</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Amber is an aromatic waxy substance secreted by whales or fossilized sap derived from coniferous trees. The former was used by humans 1000 years ago. Presently most manufacturers derive amber attar by distilling resin of ancient conifer and maturing it in sandalwood oil by following the Deg-bhapka process.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;<img alt=\"Amber Attar\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Amber_Attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Amber Attar\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Amber attar is a dark yellow perfume oil that contains natural aroma and compounds of conifer - such as sabinene, carene, pinene, and limonene. Its sweet, rich, woody, musky aroma helps alleviate mood and reduce negative feelings. It is used as a base ingredient to make aftershave and men&rsquo;s cologne. Different religious communities use it in rituals.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Saffron Attar</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Some users also know saffron attar as Zafran attar. Saffron is largely known as &lsquo;Kesar&rsquo; in India. It is a spice in the form of aromatic threads derived from the flowers of Crocus sativus. People use it to flavor and color food items, particularly milk-based products and desserts. Saffron is so far the costliest spice by weight. Kashmiri saffron is world-famous for its fragrance and taste. It is also known for its warming properties.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"saffron attar \" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/saffron_attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"saffron attar \" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The <a href=\"https://www.aromaazoils.com/traditional-indian-attars/p-saffron-attar-530.html\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>saffron attar Wholesalers in India</strong></a> distill the saffron in sandalwood oil and mature it as per the traditional attar-making process. The resultant saffron attar is a reddish perfume oil that emits a rich, sweet, intense odor. It is rich in phytochemicals, picrocrocin, and safranal compounds. Saffron attar is considered a tonic in Ayurveda. Many use it to add flavor to cuisines. The users can use it as a perfume or mix 2-3 drops in their lotions or body butter.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Rose Attar</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">As the name suggests, this attar is a rich combination of rose and sandalwood aroma. It has an intense, sweet fragrance that reduces anxiety, balances the mind, and promotes feelings of well-being. The&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/rose-attar.html\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Natural&nbsp;rose attar manufacturers</strong></a> distill the roses and mature them in sandalwood oil as per tradition and make rose attar.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Rose Attar\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Rose_Attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Rose Attar\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The devotees use it in religious rituals. Many users add it to the culinary dishes. The users popularly dab it as a perfume. They can safely add 2-3 drops of rose attar to the lotions and body butter.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Rose attar contains all the natural compounds of rose such as i-citronellol, nerol, geraniol, and compounds of sandalwood. Rose attar aroma reduces anxiety and promotes feelings of well-being.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Lily Attar</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/lily-attar.html\" target=\"_blank\">Pure Lily attar manufacturers</a> </strong>obtain lily attar by distilling flower bulbs in sandalwood oil under the traditional deg-bhapka method. Lily attar is a thick pale yellow oil with a distinct floral, sweet, lingering fragrance. It relieves stress and acts as a stimulant in the winter seasons.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Pure Lily attar\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Pure_Lily_attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Pure Lily attar\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The users can safely add it to the daily use of creams and lotions. Lily attar contains benzyl salicylate, butylphenyl, methylpropional, linalool, and other natural compounds that display antibacterial activity. The users extensively dab this attar for fragrance.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Oud Attar</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Oud attar is also known as agarwood attar. The attar manufacturers in Bengal extract this precious attar by distilling the resinous agarwood found in the trunk and root in sandalwood oil. Oud attar is a brownish, thick oil with warming, purifying, and balancing qualities. It contains caryophyllene, limonene, and camphene compounds that protect against cold and flu.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Oud attar \" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Oud_attar.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Oud attar \" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Arabian communities prefer oud attar or essential oil due to its rich, animalic, woody, and leathery notes. The users can add it to the cosmetic formulations for its anti-inflammatory properties and aroma. The perfumers employ it to create muscular fragrances. Diverse religious communities use it in rituals.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The users can experiment with other herbaceous or floral attars. Herbaceous attars include honeysuckle, kewda, sandal musk, and sandalwood shamama attars from <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Natures Natural India</strong></a>. Users, fond of particular floral fragrances, can explore pink lotus, night queen, tuberose, majmua, kadam, gulhina, frangipani, and jasmine attars.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n</div>', 1, '2022-05-14 06:21:26', '2025-01-25 06:18:58', 'indian-attars-fragrance-to-treat-to-the-world', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Indian Attars\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Indian_Attars_1.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Indian Attars\" /><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Attar is called &lsquo;Itr&rsquo; in Arabic and &lsquo;Itir&rsquo; in Persian. The attars are classified into two categories - Warm and Cool based on their perceived effect on the human body. Warm attars include black musk, ambergris, and saffron, while cool attars include rose, jasmine, khus, kewda, and mogra. The other attars are frangipani, gulhina, tagetes erecta, honeysuckle, jasmine, kadam, lily, lotus, mitti, night queen, tuberose, and shamama attars.</span></p>'),
(6, 'How to Pick Right Carrier Oils for Dry, Sore, and Inflamed Skin?', '<p class=\"normal\"><img alt=\"How To Pick Right Carrier Oils For Dry\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/How_To_Pick_Right_Carrier_Oils_For_Dry.jpg\"}}\" title=\"How To Pick Right Carrier Oils For Dry\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"></span></p>\r\n<h2 class=\"normal\"><span><strong>Review Extraction Process, Properties, Characteristics, and Types of Carrier Oils</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Carrier oils, also known as fatty-acid vegetable/base/fixed oil, are derivatives of seeds, nuts, or kernels of diverse plants. They are critical components in cosmetics and aromatherapy massage oils. Several carrier oils are available in the market, and they differ from each other in color, viscosity, penetration speed, and fatty acid profile besides rates. They affect the usefulness of the massage, color, scent, therapeutic properties, and lifespan of the final product. The selection of a carrier oil depends on the desired outcome.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Carrier oils provide the lubrication required for a massage and prevent the potential irritation, redness, sensitization, or burning caused by the undiluted use of <span style=\"color: #2a2ed4;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #2a2ed4;\"><strong>pure essential oils</strong></span></a></span>, absolutes, and CO2 extractions.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Carrier oils have individual therapeutic properties and contain fat-soluble vitamins, minerals, antioxidants, and other nutrients. They can improve the look and feel of skin and hair by adding moisture and reducing the effects of dryness.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Extraction Processes of Carrier Oils</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Cold press and expeller press are two main processes followed to extract carrier oils.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"cold-press method\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/cold-press_method.jpg\"}}\" title=\"cold-press method\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Cold Press -</span></strong> Cold pressing is a chemical-free process that involves placing high pressure on seeds, nuts, or seeds and squeezing out the oil. A filtration process takes place to get a finished oil. The cold-press process does not leave any solvent residue, so the resultant oil is cleaner, purer, and higher in natural colors and scents.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Expeller Press </span></strong>- It is a mechanical process using hydraulic pressure and heat. It is essentially a cold-press method at room or low temperatures. But when the temperature used rises above 120 degrees celsius, it is no longer a cold-press method. The manufacturers also abbreviate the term and use the RDB word for it. RDB means Refined, deodorized, and bleached. The refinement process removes impurities, improves the color and texture, or stabilizes the shelf life, making them suitable cosmetic uses.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Expeller-Press Method\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Expeller-Press_Method.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Expeller-Press Method\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Oil Maceration -</span></strong> It involves the use of botanicals holding meager oil to be obtained through a cold press. The maceration process retains the fragrances of botanical matter used in the carrier oil. In this process, botanicals are bruised and soaked in the carrier oil for a specified time. Sometimes, low heat is applied for easy infusion, and the infused liquid is filtered to obtain macerated oil with therapeutic properties of vegetable oil and the infused botanical material. Cosmetic manufacturers can use macerated oil as an ingredient for fragrance and moisture in skin care products.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Solvent extraction -</span></strong> It has three stages; soaking of botanical material, filtering of solvents, and extraction of oil. It employs solvents such as ethanol, petroleum ether, hexane, or methanol.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"Solvent-extraction method\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Solvent-extraction_method.jpg\"}}\" title=\"Solvent-extraction method\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Cosmetic manufacturers prefer to use a natural, unadulterated, cold-press oil. They assess the aroma, extraction method, consistency, absorption rate, shelf-life, natural fatty acids, and tocopherols in a carrier oil. They also evaluate the following parameters in oil to check their suitability in the end product,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Parameters for Checking Oil Suitability</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"parameters for checking oils suitability\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/parameters_for_checking_oils_suitability.jpg\"}}\" title=\"parameters for checking oils suitability\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Moisture Content </strong>- The optimum proportion of moisture content of an oil indicates the storage stability of the oil. The moisture content of 10 to 12% is desired for storage stability.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Peroxide Value</strong> - The peroxide value gives an idea about the potential rancidity of the oil. The oils with lower peroxide values are desirable.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Saponification Value </strong>- Saponification value indicates the usage potential of <span style=\"color: #4630ce;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/\"><span style=\"color: #4630ce;\"><strong>essential oil in soap making</strong></span></a></span>, degreasing, and shampoo. It has an inverse relationship with the molecular weight of the oil. The higher saponification value of the oil shows a high potential for usage in the laundry industry for soap making, degreasing, and shampoo.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Iodine Value </strong>- It is a measure of the unsaturated acids, fats, and oil present in the carrier oil. It explains the liquid nature of the oil at room temperature. A higher iodine value indicates more possibility of oxidization. The carrier oils with lower iodine values are desirable in cosmetics and edibles to ensure low reactivity.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Acid Value</strong> - Acid value indicates the potential corrosiveness of the oil. It determines its use as biodiesel, paint oil, or edible oil. The carrier oils whose acid value is less than 10 are edible. Non-corrosive, edible carrier oils are useable as biodiesel or paint oil.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>FFA (Free fatty acid)</strong> - It indicates the percentage of oleic acid of the carrier oil. The optimum proportion of oleic acid makes it a desirable ingredient in cosmetics. FFA of 1.30 &plusmn; 0.01% of bottle gourd oil is evidence of oleic acid, indicating that the oil is edible and can be applied for industrial purposes.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Other Considerations While Picking Carrier Oils</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">The manufacturers of toiletries and cosmetics also assess the nature of <span style=\"color: #4630ce;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/carrier-oils.html\"><span style=\"color: #4630ce;\"><strong>pure and natural carrier oils</strong></span></a></span>. They choose the appropriate types of carrier oils as per the product.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Types of Carrier Oils Available</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Hard Oils -</strong> These carrier oils are solid at room temperatures and provide firmness to the end products such as soap while keeping a soap bar soft or sticky. Examples of hard oils are palm and coconut. The users need to melt them down for use.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Soft Oils </strong>- They are liquid at normal temperatures, and add nourishing and moisturizing properties to a finished product. Their presence in a soap bar reduces the brittleness of soap. The popular soft oils are olive, sweet almond, argan, rice bran, and canola.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">The manufacturers substitute hard oils in place of hard oils, and the same for soft oils in a formulation. They evaluate each oil&rsquo;s contribution in preparation in terms of firmness, moisture, or even lather. If they want to reduce the hardness or softness of the end product, they may increase the ratio of soft oils or hard oils.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\">Industrial users examine the source of oils and their characteristics to pick the right carrier oil for end products.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Characteristics of Nut Oils, Seed Oils, Fruit Kernel Oils, and Fatty Acid Oils</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Nut Oils</strong> - They are excellent emollients that soothe sensitive, dry, sore, and inflamed skin. Nut oils include almond, hazelnut, macadamia, and <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/walnut-oil.html\"><strong>walnut carrier oils</strong></a>. They are ideal ingredients for anti-aging and face masks.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Seed Oils </strong>- They rejuvenate skin complexion and repair damage caused by dryness. Seed oils include baobab, black currant, borage, broccoli, and carrot seed carrier oils.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Fruit Kernel Oils</strong> - They are lightweight and do not leave a greasy residue. Fruit kernel oils include apricot, avocado, grapeseed, peach kernel, and olive carrier oils that are gentle, cleansing, softening, and nourishing.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Essential Fatty Acid Oils</strong> - These oils are argan, babassu, and calendula. They hydrate the skin and possess outstanding anti-inflammatory, antibacterial, antifungal, astringent, and antiseptic properties.</span></p>', 1, '2022-06-14 11:03:32', '2025-01-24 07:40:24', 'how-to-pick-right-carrier-oils', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"How To Pick Right Carrier Oils For Dry\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/How_To_Pick_Right_Carrier_Oils_For_Dry.jpg\"}}\" title=\"How To Pick Right Carrier Oils For Dry\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Carrier oils, also known as fatty-acid vegetable/base/fixed oil, are derivatives of seeds, nuts, or kernels of diverse plants. They are critical components in cosmetics and aromatherapy massage oils. Several carrier oils are available in the market, and they differ from each other in color, viscosity, penetration speed, and fatty acid profile besides rates. They affect the usefulness of the massage, color, scent, therapeutic properties, and lifespan of the final product. The selection of a carrier oil depends on the desired outcome.</span></p>');
INSERT INTO `aw_blog` (`post_id`, `title`, `post_content`, `status`, `created_time`, `update_time`, `identifier`, `user`, `update_user`, `meta_keywords`, `meta_description`, `comments`, `tags`, `short_content`) VALUES
(7, 'How to use Essential Oils for Personal Care? Need to know', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img height=\"388\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/essential_oil.jpg\"}}\" width=\"679\" /></span></p>\r\n<p>Essential oils are viable health and wellness alternatives. Many are multi-purpose and multi-tasking oils used for skin, hair, and health conditions. It is a myth that essential oils are fussy, girly things. In fact, essential oils are natural potions used to get a pleasant smell and improve skin and hair appearance without any gender differentiation. As men do not have as many ready-to-use cosmetics options as women, DIY recipes with essential oils for beard, hair, skin issues, relaxation, and fragrance serve the required purpose.</p>\r\n<p>Another myth about essential oils is that only feminine, floral, and sweet essential oils are available. But, in fact, there are plenty of essential oils with diverse aromas and properties produced in the world. Men prefer following essential oils for their fragrance and properties</p>\r\n<p>1. Cedarwood for Sharp, Fresh, Woody, Masculine aroma with Skin-Friendly Properties<br />2. Cinnamon for Spicy, Earthy, Woody, Sweet, fragrance with Skincare and Haircare Benefits (Lice-Killing)<br />3. Cypress for Woody, Sweet, Fruity scent and Anti-inflammatory Properties<br />4. Fir Needle for Fresh, Woody, Coniferous aroma and Anti-depressant Characteristics<br />5. Frankincense for Balsamic, Woody, Spicy, and Fruity base notes with Remarkable Scars and Stretch Marks removing Ability<br />6. Palo Santo for Sweet, Woody fragrance with Anti-Inflammatory and Immune Supporting Properties<br />7. Patchouli for its Deep, Earthy, Woody aroma and Skin-rejuvenating and Skin-healing Properties<br />8. Neroli for Exotic Floral, Lemony, Sweet odor, and Skin-beneficial Properties<br />9. Petitgrain for Fresh, Sweet, Tart, Floral aroma and Antibacterial Properties<br />10. Ylang Ylang for Rich, Sweet, Floral, Woody, Fruity fragrance and Benefits for Oily Skin<br />11. Lime for Fresh, Lemony aroma and Deodorizing Ability<br />12. Peppermint for Fresh, Minty smell and Cooling Properties</p>\r\n<p>The above list is not all-inclusive and exhaustive. Men also have the discretion to create their own blends for diverse uses. They can use them in a bath, beard grooming, hair application, skincare, fragrance, oral health, inhalation, diffuser, vaporizer, and clothing. Lightweight <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/carrier-oils.html\">carrier oils</a> such as coconut, argan, extra virgin olive oil, jojoba, avocado, and almond are critical ingredients in DIY recipes.</p>\r\n<h2>Ways to use essential oils for man</h2>\r\n<p><strong>Beard Oil</strong></p>\r\n<p>Make a beard oil by combining 20 ml of jojoba oil, 10 ml of argan oil, five drops of <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/patchouli-essential-oil.html\">patchouli essential oil</a>, three drops of cinnamon essential oil, and three drops of tea tree oil. Fill the content in a bottle with an eye-dropper. Apply it sparingly on the beard and spread it evenly. The best time to use beard oil is after a bath or face wash.<br />The male users can mix any of the essential oils (given in the list or on our website) they like after having insight into their aroma and wellness properties. We recommend including essential oils that are good in aroma and skin care and hair care benefits. As far as carrier oils are concerned, jojoba oil should be the first preference as it absorbs fast and is waxy in texture. However, users can incorporate other carrier oils in a beard oil recipe.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Beard Balm</strong></p>\r\n<p>Melt ten gms soy wax and 20 gms avocado butter and mix them, add 20 ml carrier oil (any as per user&rsquo;s discretion), three drops of cypress essential oil, four drops of neroli essential oil, and two drops of frankincense essential oil. Add this content to a small container and let it cool to make a beard balm. Apply it regularly to tame the coarse beard hair and style the beard.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>Hair Styling Gel</strong></p>\r\n<p>Dissolve one spoon of gelatin in warm water in a bowl. Add a few drops of ylang-ylang/jasmine/lemon essential oil and transfer this mixture into a glass container. Men can use it to style their hair.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><img height=\"388\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/hair_gel.jpg\"}}\" width=\"680\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>Facial Care</strong></p>\r\n<p>Take two drops of tea tree oil and five drops of jojoba oil and apply the blend to the face overnight to get rid of acne, pimples, and blackheads. Users with dark circles can use coffee oil for application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Relaxing Bath</strong></p>\r\n<p>Add a few drops of cedarwood essential oil and ylang-ylang essential oil to Epsom salt and add it to warm bath water for a refreshing and relaxing bath. The users can also directly mix essential oils in bathwater.</p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img height=\"394\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/relaxing_bath.jpg\"}}\" style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\" width=\"690\" /></p>\r\n<p><strong>Lip Balm</strong></p>\r\n<p>Heat 5 gms soy wax and five gms butter in an oven or on a low flame. Remove from the flame and add a few drops of <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/palo-santo-essential-oil.html\">palo santo essential oil</a> and 2 ml <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/carrier-oils/apricot-kernel-carrier-oil.html\">apricot kernel oil</a>. Fill this in a small airtight container and let it cool. Apply it to your lips regularly to heal chapped lips in winter.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><img height=\"393\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/lip_balm.jpg\"}}\" width=\"689\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>Deo Roll-on</strong></p>\r\n<p>Make a homemade deo roll-on with 10 ml witch hazel/rose water, five gms arrowroot powder, five gms aloe vera gel, ten gms baking soda, 10 ml distilled water, two gms magnesium hydroxide, and ten drops cypress essential oil and five drops of lemongrass essential oil. Fill the well-mixed content in an empty roll-on bottle. Apply it on the underarms and other sweating parts of the body regularly.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;\"><img height=\"393\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/deo_roll-on.jpg\"}}\" width=\"689\" /></span></p>\r\n<p>The users can add peppermint essential oil for cooling effects during summer.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Pleasant Breath</strong></p>\r\n<p>For fresh breath, add three drops of peppermint essential oil and two drops of cinnamon oil in 100 ml water and gargle with it thrice after eating twice a day to remove disagreeable odor and prevent toothache and gingivitis.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Cologne Blend</strong></p>\r\n<p>Mix 5 ml sweet almond oil, three drops of patchouli essential oil, three drops of neroli essential oil, and six drops of sandalwood essential oil in the palm. Apply the mixture on the underarms, wrists, behind knees, near earlobes, and middle of the chaste.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Moisturizer</strong></p>\r\n<p>Take 30 ml cucumber seed oil, 20 gms avocado butter, five drops cypress essential oil, and five drops palo santo essential oil. Melt the avocado butter, add other oils to it and mix them well. Fill the mixture in a bottle and apply it on exposed skin except for the face regularly to keep it hydrated<br />The users can exercise their discretion in adding different ingredients as per the consistency and aroma required in the end product. They also have to add diverse essential oils to face creams, hair oils, serums, shampoos, conditioners, shower gels, hand washes, masks, face packs, and scrubs. Besides, the <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\">essential oil manufacturers</a> also offer various ready-to-use blends for topical application, diffusion, massage, inhalation, and personal fragrance purposes.</p>\r\n<p></p>', 1, '2022-07-05 12:14:45', '2025-01-17 05:12:24', 'use-essential-oils-for-personal-care', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p><img src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/blog/essential_oil.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Essential oils are viable health and wellness alternatives. Many are multi-purpose and multi-tasking oils used for skin, hair, and health conditions. It is a myth that essential oils are fussy, girly things. In fact, essential oils are natural potions used to get a pleasant smell and improve skin and hair appearance without any gender differentiation. As men do not have as many ready-to-use cosmetics options as women, DIY recipes with essential oils for beard, hair, skin issues, relaxation, and fragrance serve the required purpose.</p>'),
(8, 'Say Hello to Radiant & Glowing Skin with Hydrosols', '<p class=\"normal\"><span><img height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Radiant_and_Glowing_Skin_with_Hydrosols.jpg\"}}\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" width=\"855\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">It is well known that we all want to get the most out of our skincare regimens. However, getting the most out of your skincare mix necessitates tailoring it to your unique requirements. Regrettably, no single product under the sun is suitable for everyone. There are certain standbys in any skincare fanatic\'s medicine cabinet among all the new cosmetic products and skincare formulae that have hit the market. There are certain components and formulations that have stood the test of time, from the most strong vitamin C and trustworthy antiaging serums to exfoliants and possibly even a moisturizing mask. But we are not pausing here, right we want more, so here it is&hellip;make your skin best in ton with the <span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><strong>blends of our essential oils</strong></span></a></span>. Some of them may contain qualities that can help with skin problems. If you want to explore essential oils that are tailored to your skin conditions, talk to your dermatologist about the following possibilities.</span></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Angelica Hydrosol:</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/angelica_hydrosol.jpg\"}}\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" width=\"855\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Angelica is a plant that grows in subarctic and temperate climates. Its origins can be traced back to France, Greenland, and Iceland. It\'s a biennial and perennial plant that\'s frequently utilized to help people detox from head to toe. Floral water is extracted without the use of chemicals from the roots and other sections of plants, making it safe to use. The translucent extract is generally obtained from the leftover Angelica essential oil due to its remarkable benefits such as antibacterial, ability to get rid of the body from detoxifying, and improving the immunity of the body. We all witness dry skin during winter and during the dry sessions. you must have used many cosmetic products, but have you ever thought about <span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/hydrosols/angelica-floral-water.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><strong>angelica floral water</strong></span></a></span>, if not give it a try, you will forget all those chemical-based cosmetic products.</span></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Basil Hydrosol:</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/basil_hydrosol.jpg\"}}\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" width=\"855\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">This is an aromatic herb that can reach a height of 0.3m to 0.5m. Basil hydrosol is a by-product of basil essential oil production. Sweet basil and holy basil are the two forms of basil that are widely used today. Any of these essential oils can be used to make this hydrosol. When properly preserved, it is quite stable. This acne-prone cream is suitable for all skin types and helps to manage blemishes, control sebum, and refine pores. This is a great toner for adding moisture to the skin\'s surface and can also be used in facial masks. <span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/hydrosols/basil-hydrosol.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><strong>Pure Organic Basil hydrosol</strong></span></a></span> has moisturizing and cooling benefits for the skin. It can be used to clean even oily-skinned teenagers.</span></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Bergamot Hydrosol:</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/bergamot_hydrosol.jpg\"}}\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" width=\"855\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bergamot orange, also known as Citrus bergamia, is a citrus fruit with a lime-like appearance. The bergamot orange, or Citrus bergamia, is a fragrant citrus fruit that is the size of an orange and has a yellow or green color comparable to a lime depending on ripeness. Bergamot Hydrosol is made by steam distilling the essential oil taken from the rinds of bergamot oranges. During the extraction procedure, the essential oil in the rind passes via water vapor before being transferred to the condensation chamber. <span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/hydrosols/bergamot-hydrosol.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><strong>Pure natural Bergamot hydrosol</strong></span></a></span>&nbsp;is produced by distilling this essential oil in the from of water. This can be applied to the neck and the entire body. It can be used in lotions and creams, as well as in wet and dry clay formulas, and it can be used to replace the water in the formulation process. This can be used as a facial toner to restore the face\'s lost charm and radiance.</span></p>\r\n<h1 class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>How to use it?</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">These can be breathed or applied to the body directly. Ingesting them is not advised. Use a patch test before applying the oils topically to your skin to ensure you\'re not allergic, and avoid using them over your eyes.</span></p>', 1, '2022-08-25 08:09:11', '2025-01-17 05:12:13', 'radiant-and-Glowing-skin-with-hydrosols', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 1, '', '<p><img height=\"488\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Radiant_and_Glowing_Skin_with_Hydrosols.jpg\"}}\" width=\"855\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">It is well known that we all want to get the most out of our skincare regimens. However, getting the most out of your skincare mix necessitates tailoring it to your unique requirements. Regrettably, no single product under the sun is suitable for everyone. There are certain standbys in any skincare fanatic\'s medicine cabinet among all the new cosmetic products and skincare formulae that have hit the market. There are certain components and formulations that have stood the test of time, from the most strong vitamin C and trustworthy antiaging serums to exfoliants and possibly even a moisturizing mask. But we are not pausing here, right we want more, so here it is&hellip;make your skin best in ton with the <span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #3366ff;\"><strong>blends of our essential oils</strong></span></a></span>. Some of them may contain qualities that can help with skin problems. If you want to explore essential oils that are tailored to your skin conditions, talk to your dermatologist about the following possibilities.</span></p>'),
(9, 'Bid farewell to acne with essential oils', '<h2><strong>What is acne?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Acne is a very common skin disorder in mostly youngsters that happens due to the clogging of hair follicles with oil and dead skin cells. It causes pimples, whiteheads, and blackheads. Teenagers are the most affected by acne, yet it affects people of all ages. Although there is a wide variety of treatments available for acne, acne can give you a hard time. The pimples and bumps take a long time to heal, and once one starts to fade, others appear. Acne can cause emotional distress as well as skin scarring, depending on its severity.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>Why essential oil&hellip;</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Scientists have recently become interested in the therapeutic potential of various natural oils. Because some data implies that essential oils have antibacterial properties, this is the case. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\">Essential oils</a></strong> are highly concentrated plant extracts. Essential oils are produced in a variety of ways by various plants. These oils are sometimes sold in their purest form by manufacturers. They dilute them in a <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/carrier-oils.html\">carrier oil</a></strong> at other times. Essential oils can be extracted in two methods. Steam or water distillation extracts the oils by forcing steam or water through the plant material. Squeezing the plant causes it to release its essential oils, which is known as cold pressing.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Eucalyptus Essential Oil</strong></h2>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/eucalyptus_oil.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Eucalyptus oil, also known scientifically as Eucalyptus Globulus, is a colorless to pale yellowish liquid with a soothing, deep, and woody-sweet aroma. Eucalyptus essential oil, eucalyptol, eucalyptus oil, fever tree, blue gum, gum tree, red gum, and stringy bark tree are some of its other names. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/eucalyptus-oil.html\">Eucalyptus Essential oil</a></strong> is frequently used in fragrances and soaps. Lotions, creams, tea, tinctures, and lozenges are some of the items made with this oil in combination with other components. It\'s also found in products for treating wounds, burns, and ulcers on the skin. More scientific research is needed on the use of eucalyptus oil or eucalyptol in the treatment of headaches and arthritis. Insecticides containing eucalyptus have been utilized in a variety of repellant sprays.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>Asafoetida Essential Oil (Hing)</strong><strong></strong></h2>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/asafoetida_oil.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/hing-asafoetida-essential-oil.html\">Asafoetida Essential Oil</a></strong> (Hing) is derived from the Umbelliferae family of plants. It is a perennial herb that can reach a height of 1 to 1.5 metres. Devil\'s dung, or jowani badian, is another name for this oil. Expectorant and sedative properties are found in this oil. It\'s popular for its anxiety-relieving properties as well as its capacity to help people lose weight. As a flavouring agent, this oil is fantastic in a variety of recipes. Because of its remarkable medical properties, this oil is in high demand on the market. It\'s great for easing menstruation discomfort and lowering blood pressure. This oil can also help you feel less bloated. It efficiently treats stomach distress and gas in the intestines. It is ideal for the treatment of gastrointestinal problems. This oil is also used to purify the blood. This oil is intended to reduce acne and give the face a healthy glow.</p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<h2><strong>Grapefruit Essential Oil</strong></h2>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/grapefruit_oil.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Grapefruit, also known as Citrus Paradisi, is a citrus tree that bears yellow-orange fruits that range in flavor from tart to sweet. The tree, which is 16-20 feet tall, has gleaming dark green foliage and white blossoms. The tree is a Mexican native. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/grapefruit-essential-oil.html\">Grapefruit Essential Oil</a></strong> is often used in aromatherapy because of its healing properties. This yellow-colored essential oil has a beneficial effect on the lymphatic system in the body and aids in the removal of pollutants.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>Risks with essential oils</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Some individuals believe essential oils are absolutely safe because they are made from natural products. Essential oils, like other natural products, do, nevertheless, pose some hazards, even when used carefully. Certain essential oils, for example, may cause allergic reactions in some people. As a result, persons who are new to essential oils should conduct a patch test to discover if they have any negative side effects, which could include: skin inflammation and burning difficulty breathing asthma attacks.</p>', 1, '2022-09-12 09:42:57', '2022-10-14 06:46:51', 'Bid-farewell-to-acne-with-essential-oils', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 0, '', '<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/2.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<h2><strong></strong></h2>\r\n<p>Acne is a very common skin disorder in mostly youngsters that happens due to the clogging of hair follicles with oil and dead skin cells. It causes pimples, whiteheads, and blackheads. Teenagers are the most affected by acne, yet it affects people of all ages. Although there is a wide variety of treatments available for acne, acne can give you a hard time. The pimples and bumps take a long time to heal, and once one starts to fade, others appear. Acne can cause emotional distress as well as skin scarring, depending on its severity.</p>'),
(10, 'CONNECTING SUSTAINABLE HEALTH WITH ESSENTIAL OILS', '<h2>WHAT IS HEALTH?</h2>\r\n<p>Individually, the definition of \'health\' can be regarded from a variety of viewpoints. Understanding how various people think about health on a personal level could give professionals useful clues about what influences behavior in the wider public when it comes to health and wellness. According to the World Health Organization, health is defined as a condition of complete physical, social, and emotional well-being, rather than simply the absence of sickness or disability. Essential oils are widely used in traditional and folk medicine all throughout the world as they help to solve various problems and work as home remedies for several health issues. Some health issues that can be cured by using essential oils are:</p>\r\n<h3>Stress Reduction</h3>\r\n<p>Many essential oils are used in aromatherapy to treat stress and anxiety in individuals. They are always considered a safe option to treat such conditions.</p>\r\n<h3>Headaches and migraines</h3>\r\n<p>People from ancient times have used essential oils to treat migraine and other types of headaches.</p>\r\n<h3>Reducing inflammation</h3>\r\n<p>Essential oils have been advised by many doctors as a possible treatment for inflammatory diseases. As they have anti-inflammatory properties.</p>\r\n<p>Essential oils are available in a wide range of quality, from natural essential oils to those mixed with less costly substances. Since there is no regulation, the label on the jar you purchase may well not list everything that\'s in it. Some of the essential oils are listed below for their unique properties.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>WORMWOOD ESSENTIAL OIL</strong>:</h2>\r\n<p>Wormwood is a herb that is used to make the alcoholic beverages vermouth and absinthe. Its oil includes thujone, a potentially toxic toxin. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\">Wormwood oil</a></strong> contains thujone, which stimulates the central nervous system and can cause seizures and other side effects. Other compounds in wormwood may help to reduce edema. People use wormwood to treat digestive issues, Crohn\'s disease, IgA nephropathy, osteoarthritis, and a variety of other ailments, however, there is no scientific evidence to back up these claims. In addition, there is no good evidence to support the use of wormwood for COVID-19. Using wormwood products that contain thujone can be dangerous.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img height=\"431\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/1.jpg\"}}\" width=\"671\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>VETIVER ESSENTIAL OIL</strong>:</h2>\r\n<p>The vetiver plant, also referred to as the khus plant, is sparse vegetation native to India that can stand up to five feet in height. Other grasses that generate essential oils, such as lemongrass and citronella, are also allied to vetiver. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/vetiver-essential-oil.html\">Vetiver oil</a></strong> has a distinctive unpleasant and rustic odor, similar to that of men\'s aftershave. Only after the roots of both the vetiver plant have developed, the essential oil is extracted through the steam distillation process and simmered in water. After that, the highly concentrated oil is scooped off the water\'s surface. Because of its relaxing and centering effects, it\'s used in holistic healing.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img height=\"473\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/2_1_.jpg\"}}\" width=\"679\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h2><strong>BLUE TANSY ESSENTIAL OIL</strong>:</h2>\r\n<p>In recent years, the blue tansy, a small flower, has garnered a lot of positive attention. As a result, it\'s become a common ingredient in a wide range of goods, from acne creams to anti-aging creams. <strong><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils/tansy-blue.html\">Blue tansy essential oil</a></strong> has also become well-known. Aromatherapists laud it for its relaxing properties. Blue tansy essential oil is presently being studied to see if it will help cure inflamed skin. There hasn\'t been much research on the usage of blue tansy oil to alleviate inflammation. However, there is some evidence that two of its key components are anti-inflammatory.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><img height=\"473\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/3_1_.jpg\"}}\" width=\"681\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<h3>Word of advice:</h3>\r\n<p>The most important element to consider when ordering essential oils is product features. However, since there is no proper system or licensing for essential oils, identifying which oils are the best can be challenging. Many businesses claim that their essential oils are \"therapeutic grade,\" but this is really a marketing word. Unfortunately, there are many goods available online or in stores that have been improperly harvested or contain ingredients not specified on the label.</p>', 1, '2022-10-14 06:32:35', '2025-01-17 05:11:51', 'Connecting-sustainable-health-with-essential-oils', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', '', '', 0, '', '<p><img src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/4.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p>Individually, the definition of \'health\' can be regarded from a variety of viewpoints. Understanding how various people think about health on a personal level could give professionals useful clues about what influences behavior in the wider public when it comes to health and wellness. According to the World Health Organization, health is defined as a condition of complete physical, social, and emotional well-being, rather than simply the absence of sickness or disability. Essential oils are widely used in traditional and folk medicine all throughout the world as they help to solve various problems and work as home remedies for several health issues. Some health issues that can be cured by using essential oils are:</p>'),
(11, 'What Are The Best Essential Oils For Massage Blends?', '<h2><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Therapeutic_Massage_Blends.jpg\"}}\" /></h2>\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<h2>Take a break and let the soothing effects of this massage blend work their magic</h2>\r\n<p>Therapeutic blends are amalgams of essential oils that work together to make the desired effect. Each oil in the blend contributes its own unique properties that help to enhance the overall impact of the blend. Overall, therapeutic blends can be a great way to promote physical and psychological health. By understanding the properties of each oil and carefully selecting the right combination of oils, you can create a powerful blend that can help to improve your overall well-being.</p>\r\n<p>All are well acquainted with spas, massage, and wellness centers. Their therapy sessions are incomplete without diverse essential oils or their blends. They provide different kinds of massages to deliver specific health benefits. The massage centers prepare unique massage oil blends taking into account different aromas and properties of distinct essential and <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/carrier-oils.html\"><strong>carrier oils</strong></a>.</p>\r\n<h2><br />They keep following things in mind while making a massage blend.</h2>\r\n<p>1. Pick an essential oil based on a specific need - mood uplifting, relaxation, or pain management.<br />2. Considering sensitivity, decide whether to diffuse, inhale, or massage particular essential oil for underlined needs.<br />3. Determine its effective combination with other essential oils. And choose one or two or no essential oils for the same and decide its proportion.<br />4. Choose the right carrier oil for quick absorption and the right impact. And determine its extent in the oil blend.<br />5. Make sure to use only pure, therapeutic-grade essential oils.<br />6. A patch test of the blend is necessary before using it to ensure there are no allergic reactions.<br />7. any potential interactivity with other health conditions, products, or medications.</p>\r\n<p>However, if you want to avail yourself of such therapy sessions at home and avoid the dilemma of picking oils or don&rsquo;t have a variety of essential oils, you can go for readymade <strong>therapeutic massage blends</strong> for different conditions. These blends are customized as per the certain needs of the users. Besides, they are also aromatic to upkeep the interest of users. But the question arises why should use such blends? The following are the benefits of using therapeutic massage blends.</p>\r\n<h1><br />Therapeutic blends benefits</h1>\r\n<p><img src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Therapeutic_Massage_Blends_Benefits.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p>1. Sound sleep: Aromatherapy is known to help improve sleep since it can relax the mind, reduce stress, and induce a calming effect.<br />2. Uplifts mood: Aromatherapy can help to improve mood by releasing hormones that can reduce stress and anxiety and help to lift spirits.<br />3. Raises concentration power: Therapeutic blends can help to improve concentration by helping to reduce stress and improve focus.<br />4. Relief from pain: Aromatherapy can relieve many types of pain, such as headaches, muscle pain, and arthritis pain.<br />5. Improves immune system: Aromatherapy can enhance the immune system as it helps to reduce stress and uplifts mood.<br />6. Improved digestion: Therapeutic blends can help to improve digestion by helping to relax the body and reduce stress.<br />7. Betterment of skin health: The natural anti-inflammatory and anti-bacterial properties of therapeutic blends can help to improve skin health and reduce skin conditions, such as acne and eczema.<br />8. Increased relaxation: Therapeutic blends can help to reduce stress a There are many different types of <strong>therapeutic essential oil blends available</strong>. Each blend is designed to target specific needs and address specific issues. Some of the most common blends are those for relaxation, stress relief, and energy support.</p>\r\n<p>Several massage blends from different <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/pure-and-natural-essential-oils.html\"><strong>essential oil manufacturers</strong></a> are available in the market.</p>\r\n<h2><br />Therapeutic Massage Blends Uses</h2>\r\n<p>1. Formation of aromatherapy candles<br />2. Creating massage oils<br />3. Making bath salts<br />4. Producing lotions and creams<br />5. Creating room sprays<br />6. Forming of roll-on perfumes<br />7. Making of body oils<br />8. Producing of soaps<br />9. Creating incense sticks<br />10.Forming skin care products</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Therapeutic_Massage_Blends_Uses.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p>Essential oil therapy has been around for centuries, but it has only recently gained popularity in the United States. Essential oil blends are becoming increasingly popular for their ability to promote relaxation, reduce stress, and improve overall well-being. There are many different types of therapeutic essential oil blends available. Each blend is designed to target specific needs and address specific issues. Some of the most common blends are those for relaxation, stress relief, and energy support.</p>\r\n<p>Relaxation blends typically contain lavender oil, roman chamomile oil, labdanum oil, vetiver, and basil essential oils. These oils have soothing effects that can help to reduce stress and promote peaceful sleep. Stress relief blends often include bergamot, Boswellia carterii, lemon, and orange essential oils. These oils are known for their calming and uplifting properties. Energy support blends usually contain peppermint, almond, pomelo, tangerine, and lemon essential oils. These essential oils are invigorating and can help to increase alertness and focus.</p>', 1, '2022-12-05 08:17:54', '2025-01-17 05:11:40', 'what-are-the-best-essential-oils-for-massage-blends', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', 'Therapeutic Massage Blends, Pure Natural Therapeutic Massage Blends, Organic Therapeutic Massage Blends, Wholesale Natural Therapeutic Massage Blends, Therapeutic Massage Blends suppliers, Therapeutic Massage Blends Wholesalers,', 'Therapeutic blends are amalgams of essential oils that work together to make the desired effect. Each oil in the blend contributes its own unique properties that help to enhance the overall impact of the blend.', 0, '', '<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Therapeutic_Massage_Blends.jpg\"}}\" /></p>'),
(12, 'Put Your Mind At Ease With Our Unique Blend of Attar', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img height=\"499\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Indian_Attars.jpg\"}}\" width=\"857\" /></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Attar has a unique role in the universe of fragrance! The Arabic term attar implies \"odors.\" Attar also referred to as Ittar, is a natural scent oil made from plants such as herbs, blooming flowers, spices, barks, and other organic sources. Only the natural distilled method is used to extract attars. After obtaining these natural oils are processed into a wood foundation, such as sandalwood, and then aged to create a lovely aroma. Depending on the plant from which the oil is obtained, the aging duration might range from one to ten years. Its amazing fragrance gives your personality a good touch-up. Many of them will improve in scent with time.</p>\r\n<h2>ITS USES</h2>\r\n<p>Attar was also once reserved for the upper class, mainly kings and queens. It is prominently used in the religious sphere. Attar can be used in a variety of ways. Attar is used as a personal perfume, especially by the Muslim population, because it contains no alcohol. In nations like Pakistan and India, rose and kewra scents are used in several sweet treats.</p>\r\n<p>In comparison to the sweets sector, the tobacco industry consumes far less attar. Kewra and rose scents are commonly used in the industry. Attars are used in the creation of scented products like cosmetics, torches, room fresheners, and incense sticks because of their enticing and natural scents.</p>\r\n<h2>TYPES OF ATTAR</h2>\r\n<p><strong>Attar is basically of two types</strong></p>\r\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>COOL ATTARS</strong>: they have a cooling effect on the human body, hence used during summer seasons.</p>\r\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>WARM ATTARS</strong>: they have a warming effect on the human body, hence used during winter seasons.</p>\r\n<h2>SOME OF THE FAMOUS ATTARS ARE GIVEN BELOW:</h2>\r\n<h3>Black Musk Attar</h3>\r\n<p><img height=\"493\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Black_Musk_Attar.jpg\"}}\" width=\"848\" /></p>\r\n<p>It has a very appealing herb and black musk fragrance, making it a vital factor in the aromatherapy and perfume industries. This oil\'s calming and energizing properties provide complete serenity and relaxation for the body, assisting in the treatment of stress, anxiety, and depressive illnesses. You can combine this yellow-brown foliage color oil with Agarwood and sandalwood oil for excellent effects. Although this oil containing <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/black-musk-attar.html\">black musk attar</a> is non-toxic and non-allergic, it is nonetheless suggested that small children and nursing women use it under the supervision of their doctors.</p>\r\n<h3>Amberi Shamama Attar</h3>\r\n<p><img height=\"496\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Amberi_Shamama_Attar.jpg\"}}\" width=\"854\" /></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/amberi-shamama-attar.html\">Hina amber attar</a> is made from more than 75 rare herbs discovered in India. The hydro-refining procedure is used to extract it. The attar is earthy in color and has a lovely fragrance. Hina is highly regarded in South Asia and the Middle East for its rich, complex, and distinctly oriental aroma. Hina is a crimson adhesive made from the leaves of the Lawsonia inermis plant, which is also known as Hina or henna in India. In India, Hina is also used as a vivifying shade on women\'s hands and feet, notably during wedding functions. It\'s a light yellowish color with a floral scent. Shamama Attar has elevated religious importance in antiquated civic institutions all throughout the world. It\'s been used for sanctuary offerings, incense, medicine, and scent.</p>\r\n<h3>Kadam attar</h3>\r\n<p><img height=\"501\" src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Kadam_Attar.jpg\"}}\" width=\"861\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Kadam tree, generally known as the Bellflower tree, is a Rubiaceae family member. In India, this bloom denotes love and knowledge, and it is regarded as a sacred tree. The blossoms come in a variety of red and orange hues. The scent of these blooms is floral and woody. The flowers are steam distilled to make Kadam attar. It contains the essential oils of Indian white sandalwood and Kadam. The <a href=\"https://www.naturesnaturalindia.com/traditional-indian-attars/kadam-attar.html\">Kadam attar</a> has a wide range of applications. It\'s a component of aromatherapy, which aids in the treatment of depression and anxiety. This is also effective in the treatment of a variety of eye diseases.</p>', 1, '2022-12-09 08:27:03', '2025-01-17 05:11:26', 'put-your-mind-at-ease-with-our-unique-blend-of-attar', 'Natures Natural', 'Natures Natural', 'Indian Attars, Indian Traditional attar, Traditional Indian Attar Supplier, Traditional Indian Attar Wholesalers, Traditional Indian Attar Manufacturers, Buy Indian Attar in Bulk, Online Traditional attar buy in Bulk', 'Attar has a special role in the universe of fragrance! The Arabic term attar implies \"odors.\" Attar also referred to as Ittar, is a natural scent oil made from plants.', 0, '', '<p><img src=\"{{media url=\"wysiwyg/Indian_Attars.jpg\"}}\" /></p>\r\n<p>Attar has a unique role in the universe of fragrance! The Arabic term attar implies \"odors.\" Attar also referred to as Ittar, is a natural scent oil made from plants such as herbs, blooming flowers, spices, barks, and other organic sources. Only the natural distilled method is used to extract attars. After obtaining these natural oils are processed into a wood foundation, such as sandalwood, and then aged to create a lovely aroma. Depending on the plant from which the oil is obtained, the aging duration might range from one to ten years. Its amazing fragrance gives your personality a good touch-up. Many of them will improve in scent with time.</p>'),
